.agents/

# Git worktrees. A worktree directory holds a full second copy of the source and
# must never be committed. `.worktrees/group-chat-media` WAS tracked (as a
# gitlink), which is why that stale copy kept turning up in greps, in file
# searches and in `tsc --noEmit` output — and the workaround was to exclude it by
# hand in every command. Untracked and ignored instead.
.worktrees/
